{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md; cat lib/main.dart; command -v flutter; command -v dart'","aggregated_output":"# kredito\n\nFlutter app (iOS + Android) for a consumer loan broker. The user registers\nwith an email and a phone number, picks the amount they want to borrow, accepts\nthe terms and gets a list of offers from partner banks. Two screens so far:\n`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`.\n\nAnalytics is PostHog (`posthog_flutter`), set up in `lib/analytics.dart` and\n`lib/main.dart`; screen views come from `PosthogObserver`. We are on the\nPostHog free tier. Product events are defined in `docs/EVENTS.md`; the\nscreens do not send any of them yet. Send events through `Analytics.capture`\nso the key and host stay in one place.\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nimport 'analytics.dart';\nimport 'screens/offer_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/registration_screen.dart';\n\nFuture<void> main() async {\n  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();\n  await Analytics.init();\n  runApp(const KreditoApp());\n}\n\nclass KreditoApp extends StatelessWidget {\n  const KreditoApp({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return PostHogWidget(\n      child: MaterialApp(\n        title: 'Kredito',\n        theme: ThemeData(colorSchemeSeed: Colors.green, useMaterial3: true),\n        navigatorObservers: [PosthogObserver()],\n        routes: {\n          '/': (_) => const RegistrationScreen(),\n          '/offers': (_) => const OfferScreen(),\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/development/flutter/bin/flutter\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/development/flutter/bin/dart\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
